// Soils (v2 §5.3): climate × parent rock × vegetation × drainage × slope. The world generator
// picks, for each land column, the soil whose formation fits best (listed climates, parent
// rocks and drainage must match; vegetation adds to the fit) and lays its horizons as blocks,
// thinned on steep ground. Horizon thicknesses are real metres (a block is a metre); horizons
// thinner than half a block are part of the turf. Fertility is a simplified 0–1 N/P/K/organic
// scale.
//
// Climates are Köppen codes or their prefixes ("D" = all continental, "Cs" = mediterranean).
// Vegetation words the generator understands: broadleaf_forest, mixed_forest, boreal_forest,
// montane_forest, tropical_forest, temperate_rainforest, grassland, steppe, savanna, scrub,
// desert, tundra, alpine, wetland, floodplain.
